PATCH 560: complete patch 407 -- the other four SMC'd colormap-offset reads.

The extender's terrain renderer is SELF-MODIFYING: the map-load setup writes the map's detail and its
derived sizes directly into the raycaster's instruction immediates.  From asm 0x8a7a onward:

    8a7a: a1 90 84 00 00   mov  0x8490,%eax      ; the detail (9..12)
    8a7f: a2 66 6d 00 00   mov  %al,0x6d66       ; -> the imm8 of `shld $0xa` at 0x6d63
    8a84: a2 6a 6d 00 00   mov  %al,0x6d6a       ; ... and ~30 more shift immediates across the
    ...                                          ;     whole terrain pipeline (0x6ae6, 0x7fc7,
    8b10: a2 34 94 00 00   mov  %al,0x9434       ;     0x8f48, 0x9068, 0x8485, 0x9429, ...)
    8b15: a1 98 84 00 00   mov  0x8498,%eax      ; the colormap offset = dim*dim
    8b1a: a3 9d 6d 00 00   mov  %eax,0x6d9d      ; -> the disp32 of the colour read at 0x6d9a
    8b1f: a3 1d 6e 00 00   mov  %eax,0x6e1d
    8b24: a3 1d 6b 00 00   mov  %eax,0x6b1d
    8b29: a3 9d 6b 00 00   mov  %eax,0x6b9d

so the `shld $0xa` and `+0x100000` that a static disassembly shows are DEFAULTS, not the running
values.  On these maps (`detail[0x8490]=0xb`, `dim=2048`) they become 0xb and 0x400000.

Exactly four colour reads are patched, in `FUN_0000_6b03`, `FUN_0000_6b83`, `FUN_0000_6d83` and
`FUN_0000_6e03`.  Patch 407 ("6980-smc-dynamic") already converted the SMC-dependent code in
`FUN_0000_6977` to read `DAT_0000_8490` / `DAT_0000_8498` instead of the baked literals -- and the port
does compute both correctly (`build/fist_ext.c`: `bRam00006ae6 = detail`, `DAT_0000_8494 = 1 << detail`,
`iRam00006b1d = dim*dim`, `DAT_0000_8498 = iRam00006b1d`).  But 407 stopped at 6977; the other four
functions still carry the literal `0x100000`, so on a 2048-square map they would read colours from
1 MB into the heightmap instead of from the colormap at 4 MB.

This patch applies 407's own fix to the remaining eight sites (two per function).

MEASURED, and the reason this is not claimed as a render fix: it changes nothing on the paths currently
exercised.  AZER1 with FIST_TERRAIN=1 gives full-frame AE 29306 before and 29311 after against
ref/mission_azer1_cockpit_native320.png, i.e. the four functions are not the ones running there --
6977 is, and 407 already covers it.  The change is landed because it is asm-verified and because
leaving a known-wrong literal in code the SMC explicitly parameterises is exactly the latent-defect
shape this cascade keeps producing: wrong until something makes it reachable, then wrong loudly.

board:0002

